**Design Explanation**  
The D latch implements a simple storage element where the output follows the input 'd' when enabled by 'ena'. The always block uses a sensitivity list to detect changes in both 'ena' and 'd', ensuring the output updates immediately when either input changes. The if-else structure within the always block ensures the output reflects the current input value when enabled, maintaining the stored value when disabled.

[BEGIN]
module TopModule(
  input  d,
  input  ena,
  output q
);

  always @(ena or d) begin
    if (ena)
      q = d;
    else
      q = q;
  end
endmodule
